  "id": "COMPOUND:30040 - PROTEIN:5792",
  "verbalization": "Basiliskamide B is shown to interact with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a key enzyme in the sialylation pathway. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate, both of which are known to have targets in the RWLeu4 pathway. The shared target of these compounds suggests a potential mechanism by which Basiliskamide B may influence RWLeu4 through the sialylation process. The evidence indicates that Basiliskamide B may act through a pathway involving sialylation, potentially modulating RWLeu4 by affecting the enzymatic activity of the sialyltransferase. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Basiliskamide B in regulating RWLeu4 through a complex, multi-step biochemical process that involves the sialylation of specific substrates.",
